Luxel local patch (Gitea #460 / #789): a per-plane REPEAT SCHEDULE for the
BCM descriptor chain, so the caller can emit low bitplanes once (with OE
cut off early in the framebuffer words) instead of `2^k` times.

Applies on top of the dma-position patch. Mechanism: a crate-level static
`PLANE_REPEATS` (one `AtomicU8` per plane, 0 = the stock `2^(planes-1-idx)`),
set by `set_plane_repeats(&[u8])` BEFORE `Hub75::new`; `fill_full_chain`
reads it for every ring it builds (the initial ring and the lazily built
second ring alike), and `CircularBcmBuf::new` sizes the ring with the new
`dma_descriptor_count_scheduled`. `max_dma_chunk_size()` exposes the chunk
size so a caller can size its own descriptor slice for the schedule.
Nothing in the ISR changes: both rings are built with the same counts, so
the ring stride, `desc_count` and the pass arithmetic stay consistent —
which is also why the counts must not change while a driver is running.
The linear (non-`circular-dma`) builder keeps the stock arithmetic.

